WEBVTT

00:02.250 --> 00:06.790
With the third semester drawing to a close,
one thing happened that made me happy.

00:07.460 --> 00:11.000
I managed to get through finals
without my grades taking a hit,

00:11.210 --> 00:13.290
so my video games weren't confiscated.

00:13.920 --> 00:16.960
It's raining outside, but my mind is clear.

00:17.420 --> 00:18.580
Shiraishi-kun.

00:20.540 --> 00:22.670
Did something good happen?

00:23.380 --> 00:24.960
Uh, why?

00:25.250 --> 00:27.080
Well, no reason.

00:28.130 --> 00:29.750
Um, thanks.

00:29.750 --> 00:30.500
Huh?

00:31.420 --> 00:36.750
Thanks to your tutoring, I managed to survive finals.

00:37.460 --> 00:40.540
That's great! Let's study together again sometime.

00:40.790 --> 00:41.500
Uh...

00:41.670 --> 00:42.500
What?

00:43.040 --> 00:46.130
Well, our classes are changing soon.

00:46.750 --> 00:50.710
That's right. When the new school year starts, everyone
gets separated into different classes.

00:51.380 --> 00:52.130
Uh-huh.

00:54.790 --> 00:56.250
It's raining.

00:56.830 --> 00:57.830
Yeah, it is.

00:59.210 --> 01:03.750
Thus, the days I'm found by Kubo-san
may soon be over too.

01:05.920 --> 01:08.710
Please, just for a moment

01:08.710 --> 01:12.750
Let the time freeze

01:14.920 --> 01:18.330
When did it start?

01:18.330 --> 01:22.000
I cannot remember

01:22.830 --> 01:26.580
Who actually cares?

01:26.580 --> 01:29.330
"It doesn't matter"

01:29.880 --> 01:32.920
Laughing or shedding tears

01:32.920 --> 01:37.040
Whenever we realized

01:37.500 --> 01:43.000
Or too persistent to take in sometime

01:44.380 --> 01:54.290
Ready? And go as the traffic light changes (As we are)

01:54.290 --> 01:58.250
No words needed (as far as we can be)

01:58.420 --> 02:01.380
we can surely make it

02:01.380 --> 02:05.040
Even if it wasn't dramatic

02:05.210 --> 02:08.880
Even if it was boring and I was moaning

02:09.170 --> 02:14.080
I'll remember this day

02:14.540 --> 02:15.540
When? I don't know

02:16.080 --> 02:19.790
I don't need no romantic words

02:19.960 --> 02:23.380
I just want one thing

02:23.460 --> 02:26.170
Let the time freeze

02:26.170 --> 02:30.080
Just for a moment...

02:30.580 --> 02:32.500
The words fell

02:35.710 --> 02:40.290
<b>Episode 7: Sleepover and Next School Year</b>

02:36.210 --> 02:38.250
It's a good thing I brought my umbrella!

02:38.710 --> 02:40.380
Shiraishi-kun, did you bring one?

02:40.500 --> 02:44.920
No. The weather report said it wouldn't
start raining until this evening.

02:47.040 --> 02:49.580
Ah, okay. That's perfect.

02:50.380 --> 02:51.420
What's perfect?

02:51.960 --> 02:53.080
I've got a bad feeling about this.

02:55.500 --> 02:57.170
Let's do an experiment!

02:57.830 --> 02:58.830
An experiment?

02:58.830 --> 03:05.170
If we stand under an umbrella together,
will other people notice you? Or not?

03:07.040 --> 03:08.170
That'd be fun, right?

03:09.500 --> 03:10.250
Huh?

03:11.460 --> 03:13.960
People would totally see me.

03:13.960 --> 03:15.420
Have you ever tried it before?

03:16.080 --> 03:16.960
I haven't.

03:19.130 --> 03:20.670
Then let's give it a shot!

03:21.130 --> 03:22.420
Not happening.

03:29.880 --> 03:32.130
Here! I'm lending you mine.

03:33.080 --> 03:35.170
Kubo-san? What are you doing?

03:40.170 --> 03:42.580
Shiraishi-kun, use my umbrella on your way home.

03:42.580 --> 03:44.080
I'll run home.

03:44.750 --> 03:45.330
What?

03:45.920 --> 03:47.290
Later, Shiraishi-kun!

03:47.580 --> 03:48.330
Huh?

03:56.460 --> 03:58.080
I can't let you do that.

04:00.380 --> 04:02.000
Then let the experiment begin!

04:02.290 --> 04:03.130
Sigh...

04:03.500 --> 04:05.630
What if someone sees us?

04:07.290 --> 04:11.670
She called it an experiment,
but all the same, this situation is...

04:13.500 --> 04:16.580
I gotta be mindful of our
shoulders brushing and whatnot.

04:17.330 --> 04:18.080
Wait.

04:18.380 --> 04:19.880
Are we actually...

04:20.630 --> 04:21.790
Sharing an umbrella as a coup-

04:26.750 --> 04:27.880
What's wrong?

04:28.790 --> 04:32.790
Crap. She camouflaged this as an experiment
so I didn't realize it, but we're...

04:33.250 --> 04:35.290
Sharing an umbrella like couples do.

04:36.250 --> 04:36.960
We're...

04:37.630 --> 04:39.170
Totally sharing an umbrella like a couple!

04:38.830 --> 04:41.420
<b>Shiraishi's</b>

04:38.830 --> 04:41.420
<b>words</b>

04:38.830 --> 04:41.420
<b>failed</b>

04:38.840 --> 04:41.420
<b>him.</b>

04:42.080 --> 04:45.880
We need to take an empty street so no one else sees us.

04:47.540 --> 04:49.210
Hey, Kubo-san.

04:49.210 --> 04:51.420
Is it okay if we take this way home?

04:52.290 --> 04:53.170
Sounds good to me!

04:53.420 --> 04:54.330
All right!

04:54.920 --> 04:57.920
This is a narrow street that doesn't get a lot of foot traffic.

04:58.290 --> 04:59.920
Plus, it's raining.

05:03.290 --> 05:06.330
We won't run into anyone else at this time.

05:10.670 --> 05:12.710
<b>Pedestrian</b>

05:10.670 --> 05:12.710
<b>and cyclist</b>

05:10.670 --> 05:12.710
<b>use only</b>

05:12.920 --> 05:16.210
Aww, we didn't see anyone else.

05:16.420 --> 05:18.540
We weren't able to do the experiment.

05:18.830 --> 05:20.500
We're already almost home.

05:21.580 --> 05:22.580
Yeah, you're right.

05:23.210 --> 05:26.080
Phew! We managed not to bump into anyone else.

05:26.080 --> 05:27.380
Hey, Shiraishi-kun.

05:27.920 --> 05:29.580
Wh-what?

05:31.330 --> 05:35.380
It was just the two of us the whole way home.
Was that maybe intentional?

05:35.880 --> 05:36.710
Intentional?

05:38.630 --> 05:39.290
Ah.

05:40.080 --> 05:40.790
Ah...

05:41.250 --> 05:41.960
Ah.

05:44.880 --> 05:46.170
Shiraishi-kun?

05:47.630 --> 05:49.250
I didn't plan it to be that way.

05:50.750 --> 05:52.420
We should walk home together again sometime.

05:52.920 --> 05:56.960
<b>Pedestrian</b>

05:52.920 --> 05:56.960
<b>and cyclist</b>

05:52.920 --> 05:56.960
<b>use only</b>

05:54.420 --> 05:55.080
M'kay?

05:55.880 --> 05:56.540
Okay.

06:00.830 --> 06:02.380
Aww, you're such a cutie.

06:07.960 --> 06:09.000
Oh?

06:10.210 --> 06:12.080
Ah, to be young!

06:14.670 --> 06:16.290
Sorry. My house is here.

06:16.290 --> 06:18.540
Okay. We're also close to my house.

06:19.630 --> 06:20.540
Thank you.

06:21.000 --> 06:22.130
No problem.

06:24.130 --> 06:25.500
See you later, Shiraishi-kun.

06:25.960 --> 06:26.670
Yeah.

06:33.040 --> 06:33.960
I'm home!

06:35.250 --> 06:38.040
Welcome back! Were you okay in the rain?

06:38.460 --> 06:39.630
Yeah, I was fine.

06:40.290 --> 06:40.960
Oh?

06:41.670 --> 06:43.040
It doesn't look like that's the case.

06:43.290 --> 06:44.630
What's wrong with your umbrella?

06:45.130 --> 06:46.250
Nothing really.

06:52.130 --> 06:53.290
I'm home!

06:56.460 --> 06:58.460
Welcome back. You sure are late.

06:58.830 --> 07:00.750
Huh? Why do you say that?

07:00.750 --> 07:02.040
Isn't this the normal time I get back?

07:02.460 --> 07:05.040
Oh, well, it doesn't matter.

07:05.920 --> 07:07.920
Oh, by the way, are you free this Saturday?

07:08.460 --> 07:10.460
Saki wants to hang out again.

07:10.460 --> 07:12.540
Yeah, I'm free.

07:12.790 --> 07:14.210
Then it's settled!

07:15.540 --> 07:21.080
<b>The Honest Basket</b>

07:24.210 --> 07:27.040
Huh? Is that... Saki-chan?

07:27.880 --> 07:29.630
She's carrying a lot of bags.

07:29.630 --> 07:31.000
It looks like she's struggling.

07:33.040 --> 07:33.960
Hey there.

07:34.380 --> 07:36.000
Are you going far with those?

07:37.920 --> 07:40.540
I'll give you a hand. Those look heavy.

07:44.210 --> 07:47.170
Oh, do you remember me?

07:47.460 --> 07:50.920
I remember you. You're Shiraishi-san, right?

07:50.920 --> 07:52.920
Ah, yes, that's right.

07:53.880 --> 07:56.540
I'm okay. I can carry it by myself.

07:57.710 --> 07:59.830
I wanna carry it! I'm stwong!

07:59.830 --> 08:02.920
She reminds me of Seita when
he's dead set on carrying something.

08:03.670 --> 08:08.130
They are heavy. But if I carry them back all by myself,

08:08.420 --> 08:11.080
Nagi-chan will definitely praise me since they're heavy.

08:16.250 --> 08:18.290
She might praise you,

08:18.420 --> 08:21.960
but she'll feel just as much worry as pride, I'd imagine.

08:22.380 --> 08:24.540
Really, she will?

08:25.630 --> 08:29.040
I'll tell her you carried them all on your own. All right?

08:32.790 --> 08:36.000
When we get close to Nagi-chan's house,
I'll take them back.

08:36.000 --> 08:37.250
O-okay.

08:37.790 --> 08:38.630
Well then, let's go.

08:39.290 --> 08:41.330
They're heavier than I thought they'd be.

08:41.830 --> 08:43.170
What's in these bags?

08:43.540 --> 08:45.040
<b>Rice For One</b>

08:46.130 --> 08:47.380
<b>Hishimatsu</b>

08:46.130 --> 08:47.380
<b>Soy Sauce</b>

08:48.670 --> 08:49.500
Were you running errands?

08:49.500 --> 08:50.380
No.

08:51.130 --> 08:56.080
I learned how to make meat and potato stew,
so I thought I'd make Nagi-chan lunch.

08:56.420 --> 08:57.670
That's impressive.

08:57.670 --> 09:01.920
Nagi-chan said she'd prepare the ingredients,

09:02.580 --> 09:05.080
but her cooking skills are...

09:05.670 --> 09:09.580
Somewhat dubious, so I bought extra.

09:10.670 --> 09:14.420
But that's part of what makes her an angel.

09:11.710 --> 09:14.420
They're not relying on Kubo-san.

09:17.920 --> 09:22.750
But I couldn't buy sake and mirin,
so we may not be able to make it.

09:24.460 --> 09:29.170
Do people normally have sake and
mirin at home, Shiraishi-san?

09:30.880 --> 09:32.250
Shiraishi-san?

09:34.630 --> 09:36.080
What's mirin?

09:39.080 --> 09:40.960
Lemme ask Kubo-san.

09:41.670 --> 09:42.580
Okay.

09:43.290 --> 09:47.290
Saki said she'd be here at eleven,
but she's already thirty minutes late!

09:47.290 --> 09:50.920
It's no biggie. She'll be here soon.

09:51.290 --> 09:53.540
If it was me, I'd be an hour late.

09:54.000 --> 09:56.210
Comparing the two of you is
like comparing apples and oranges!

09:56.750 --> 09:58.250
I'm going out to look for her!

09:58.250 --> 09:59.250
M'kay!

10:00.130 --> 10:01.420
Where's Saki?

10:03.460 --> 10:03.960
<b>Now</b>

10:03.460 --> 10:03.960
<b>Shiraishi</b>

10:03.460 --> 10:03.960
<b>Text Message</b>

10:03.960 --> 10:07.750
<b>Shiraishi-kun</b>

10:03.960 --> 10:07.750
<b>Do you have mirin and sake at home?</b>

10:03.960 --> 10:07.750
<b>Saki-chan is worrying about it</b>

10:05.750 --> 10:07.380
Why is Shiraishi-kun asking me this?

10:11.250 --> 10:14.250
<b>Kubo-san</b>

10:11.250 --> 10:14.250
<b>Do you have mirin and sake at home?</b>

10:11.250 --> 10:14.250
<b>Saki-chan is worrying about it</b>

10:11.250 --> 10:14.250
<b>Read</b>

10:11.250 --> 10:14.250
<b>Kubo-san</b>

10:11.250 --> 10:14.250
<b>I asked Akina, and she said we have</b>

10:11.260 --> 10:14.250
<b>both mirin cooking wine and sake</b>

10:12.250 --> 10:13.960
Ah, it sounds like they have some.

10:15.290 --> 10:17.330
I've been meaning to ask you something.

10:17.330 --> 10:18.130
Hmm?

10:18.460 --> 10:21.830
How close are you and Nagi-chan?

10:22.210 --> 10:24.080
H-how close we are?

10:24.080 --> 10:25.580
Are you her boyfriend?

10:25.580 --> 10:27.080
No, I'm not.

10:27.460 --> 10:28.920
Are you best friends?

10:29.330 --> 10:30.000
No.

10:30.000 --> 10:31.670
Are you friends?

10:32.750 --> 10:34.830
We're just classmates, I guess.

10:37.000 --> 10:38.580
Shiraishi-san...

10:40.790 --> 10:42.130
She's looking at me with pity.

10:42.580 --> 10:45.290
So you're not close.

10:45.290 --> 10:46.250
Or not!

10:47.250 --> 10:49.790
I call her Nagi-chan.

10:49.790 --> 10:50.830
That's right.

10:50.830 --> 10:54.380
And Nagi-chan calls me Saki.

10:54.380 --> 10:55.790
Y-yeah, I'm aware.

10:56.080 --> 10:57.670
We're close!

11:01.130 --> 11:05.880
Could it be that you're not close enough
to even know her first name?

11:05.880 --> 11:08.750
Of course I know her first name.

11:09.580 --> 11:11.250
So say it.

11:12.710 --> 11:13.630
Um...

11:13.630 --> 11:15.790
See! You can't even say it.

11:16.920 --> 11:17.790
Saki!

11:19.630 --> 11:20.420
Nagi-chan!

11:20.420 --> 11:22.830
What a relief! I was worried.

11:23.670 --> 11:25.540
Thank you, Shiraishi-kun.

11:26.000 --> 11:26.920
It was nothing.

11:27.210 --> 11:28.290
I've been saved!

11:29.710 --> 11:34.960
I think Shiraishi-san doesn't know
your first name, Nagi-chan.

11:34.960 --> 11:37.460
What? There's no way he...

11:38.330 --> 11:42.790
Ah! Now that you mention it,
I was also worried he might not know it.

11:44.290 --> 11:46.830
O-of course I know your first name.

11:48.210 --> 11:50.000
If you do, then say it.

11:51.750 --> 11:52.710
...Right?

11:52.960 --> 11:56.330
I can't hear you! Say it a little louder.

11:59.290 --> 12:02.880
Na... Nagisa, right?

12:06.580 --> 12:09.710
Speaking of which, do you know
Shiraishi-kun's first name, Saki?

12:09.710 --> 12:12.460
Yes. Shiraishi's first name is...

12:14.500 --> 12:15.920
She forgot.

12:17.960 --> 12:21.500
Shiraishi-kun's first name is Junta.

12:23.960 --> 12:25.880
Thanks for carrying the bags all the way here.

12:25.880 --> 12:27.330
Oh, no problem.

12:27.830 --> 12:29.380
See you later, Shiraishi-kun.

12:29.830 --> 12:30.580
Yeah.

12:40.130 --> 12:44.290
He said they're less than friends and only classmates.

12:47.170 --> 12:49.250
Shiraishi-san is a liar.

12:51.000 --> 12:55.000
<b>I'm upset!!</b>

12:51.000 --> 12:55.000
<b>And also Saki-chan</b>

12:56.500 --> 12:58.130
It's pollen season.

13:05.080 --> 13:06.630
Oh, Shiraishi.

13:07.170 --> 13:08.670
He's here today.

13:09.960 --> 13:14.830
I surprise the people around me
and become more visible to them.

13:18.330 --> 13:26.960
Okay, this is a very important, fundamental
concept, so study and remember it.

13:22.670 --> 13:24.960
I'm in class, but I'm bored.

13:27.710 --> 13:30.330
Fellow boys, does this ever happen to you?

13:30.880 --> 13:33.290
You're feeling sort of bored,

13:33.750 --> 13:36.000
so you disassemble a ballpoint pen.

13:36.920 --> 13:40.170
Incidentally, my favorite part is the spring.

13:41.380 --> 13:44.080
That's the part that makes the pen click.

13:45.380 --> 13:47.540
Then, when you're playing with the spring...

13:47.540 --> 13:48.290
Oh!

13:51.330 --> 13:53.830
Have you ever lost it on accident?

13:55.540 --> 13:56.750
I have.

13:59.670 --> 14:00.880
Kubo-san is...

14:03.920 --> 14:07.290
Looking at me with a deeply perplexed expression.

14:09.460 --> 14:11.210
How long has she been watching me?

14:11.210 --> 14:14.080
I've been watching since around the time
you started taking apart the pen.

14:14.080 --> 14:15.790
She even read my mind!

14:16.670 --> 14:18.580
Why'd you take it apart?

14:18.580 --> 14:19.710
That's the million-dollar question!

14:20.290 --> 14:22.630
I'm sorta curious how it works?

14:23.170 --> 14:24.290
Okay then.

14:24.630 --> 14:26.380
She doesn't seem convinced.

14:27.130 --> 14:28.960
Is your red pen broken?

14:29.670 --> 14:30.500
Yeah.

14:31.210 --> 14:35.420
I'd put it back together if I could find the spring,
but I don't know where it is.

14:35.920 --> 14:40.040
Well, I should be fine without it for one day.

14:41.040 --> 14:42.540
All right!

14:42.540 --> 14:45.710
It's time to check everyone's answers on the homework.

14:45.710 --> 14:47.420
Get your red pens out!

14:47.420 --> 14:48.960
I'm already in a bind!

14:50.580 --> 14:51.710
What'll I do?

14:54.330 --> 14:55.960
Do you want me to give you a red pen?

14:58.960 --> 15:01.130
You'd be doing me a solid,
but did you say you're giving it to me?

15:01.130 --> 15:02.330
You're not lending it to me?

15:02.330 --> 15:04.290
Yeah, you can have it.

15:04.290 --> 15:06.540
I really appreciate it, but are you sure?

15:06.750 --> 15:09.460
It's about to run out of ink anyway, so it's fine.

15:09.830 --> 15:11.040
Oh, okay.

15:11.830 --> 15:14.290
I also have a fresh pen.

15:14.290 --> 15:16.080
Kubo-san is really nice.

15:16.920 --> 15:18.040
Here you go!

15:19.960 --> 15:20.920
Than-

15:23.080 --> 15:24.630
It's ultra cute!

15:25.880 --> 15:27.670
It's kinda...

15:27.670 --> 15:30.710
You're thinking it's too cute for you, right?

15:31.000 --> 15:32.130
She hit the nail on the head.

15:32.460 --> 15:35.880
But your red pen broke so you have to use it, huh?

15:37.710 --> 15:38.880
Yeah, I do.

15:38.880 --> 15:41.210
Yep. Don't take it apart.

15:41.540 --> 15:43.130
No way I'd do that.

15:43.130 --> 15:44.630
I have my doubts.

15:53.460 --> 15:54.670
Shiraishi-kun.

15:56.710 --> 15:58.000
We match.

16:02.960 --> 16:05.420
Use it until it's out of ink, m'kay?

16:06.040 --> 16:06.920
Okay.

16:06.920 --> 16:10.290
All right, how was that? Did you get that one right?

16:10.290 --> 16:16.000
Next up, let's try our hands at
the last question, question six.

16:17.040 --> 16:20.830
This one's a trick question.

16:27.380 --> 16:27.880
Hey.

16:27.880 --> 16:28.380
Yeah?

16:28.380 --> 16:29.420
You taught me that yesterday.

16:29.420 --> 16:29.880
Yep.

16:29.880 --> 16:30.630
You're the man!

16:30.630 --> 16:31.210
You know it.

16:32.670 --> 16:36.500
Oh, hey. There are refill cartridges for that pen,
so you can use it forever.

16:36.920 --> 16:39.790
What? Then why'd you buy another one?

16:40.170 --> 16:44.040
I only learned there are refill cartridges
after I bought the new one.

16:44.960 --> 16:45.920
Ah, gotcha.

16:50.920 --> 16:54.380
It's our last day as a class together.

16:54.380 --> 16:56.330
I don't wanna switch classes.

16:56.330 --> 16:58.000
I really don't either.

16:59.000 --> 17:01.880
When we become second-year students,
our classes change.

16:59.420 --> 17:02.290
Hey, what should I bring today?

17:02.540 --> 17:06.080
That being said, it makes no difference to me.

17:02.670 --> 17:05.460
Oh, right. I didn't ask about that.

17:06.170 --> 17:07.960
Is there anything I should buy and bring?

17:07.960 --> 17:11.630
Nah, no need. My parents are
setting us up with provisions.

17:11.630 --> 17:13.540
Ah, I'm so excited!

17:20.210 --> 17:23.460
<b>Kudo</b>

17:24.460 --> 17:26.210
Tonight, we're...

17:27.830 --> 17:29.920
Having a sleepover!

17:32.580 --> 17:35.380
Hey, how'd finals go for you two?

17:35.380 --> 17:37.130
Same as usual, I guess.

17:37.130 --> 17:39.080
Ah, okay.

17:40.250 --> 17:41.210
How about you, Tama?

17:41.210 --> 17:43.920
Since you brought up the topic, did you do pretty good?

17:46.290 --> 17:48.210
I'm glad you asked.

17:48.790 --> 17:50.130
If I'm being honest...

17:51.670 --> 17:54.000
I failed one!

17:54.750 --> 17:56.670
Wow, go you!

17:58.170 --> 18:01.790
Wait. Why do you look so proud
about failing a final exam?

18:01.960 --> 18:04.500
It's a new best record for me!

18:04.960 --> 18:07.830
Slowly but surely, Tama's failing fewer exams!

18:07.830 --> 18:11.460
At this rate, I won't fail any exams
or need remedial lessons next time!

18:18.080 --> 18:19.790
Good job.

18:22.920 --> 18:25.170
Hey, is it cool if I open the snacks?

18:25.630 --> 18:26.920
Yeah, go ahead.

18:30.130 --> 18:31.380
This is so yummy!

18:32.080 --> 18:32.920
Delicious!

18:35.750 --> 18:38.540
Don't be flustered, Tama!

18:42.080 --> 18:43.330
Yeah!

18:43.330 --> 18:45.130
What, how funny!

18:48.290 --> 18:50.380
It's already midnight! That was quick!

18:50.380 --> 18:51.290
Sure was!

18:51.290 --> 18:52.540
I'll get the futon out.

18:52.540 --> 18:53.580
I'll help!

18:53.580 --> 18:54.330
Okay!

19:01.380 --> 19:03.630
We're gonna be second-year students before we know it!

19:04.080 --> 19:06.500
Our first year of high school went by in a flash.

19:07.210 --> 19:09.330
So true. It went by just like that.

19:09.960 --> 19:12.330
Which means we're changing classes soon.

19:16.710 --> 19:18.790
N-no!

19:19.250 --> 19:22.500
Tama, it's not a sure thing that we'll be separated.

19:24.000 --> 19:27.500
If we end up in different classes,
we won't have as much time together.

19:28.130 --> 19:30.170
I'll miss you two so much!

19:34.290 --> 19:37.080
Saying that made me feel lonely.

19:37.080 --> 19:38.250
Can we hug?

19:38.920 --> 19:40.830
You already are.

19:40.830 --> 19:42.080
Exactly.

19:43.630 --> 19:47.460
But we still have sports day, the cultural festival,

19:47.460 --> 19:52.790
and also the ball game tournament,
and then there's the camping trip and the field trip.

19:52.790 --> 19:54.040
I wanna do them all together.

19:58.210 --> 20:02.960
Yeah. Doing them with everyone would be fun.

20:04.290 --> 20:07.540
Speaking of which, are you including Shiraishi in that?

20:08.420 --> 20:10.040
Why Shiraishi-kun?

20:11.080 --> 20:14.250
Kubocchi, you talk about Shiraishi quite a bit.

20:14.250 --> 20:17.250
I thought you'd want to be in the same class as him.

20:17.830 --> 20:18.460
So do you?

20:20.960 --> 20:21.960
Not in particular.

20:23.880 --> 20:25.580
It doesn't matter whether we are or not.

20:30.580 --> 20:32.630
Argh! I'm going to sleep!

20:33.210 --> 20:35.920
No! I'm not letting you sleep tonight!

20:35.920 --> 20:38.580
C'mon, I said I'm going to sleep!

20:38.580 --> 20:40.290
There now, don't be like that.

20:40.710 --> 20:42.790
Give me some space, Tama!

20:43.080 --> 20:45.130
I can't fall asleep!

20:47.130 --> 20:51.670
She said she wasn't gonna let us sleep,
but she ended up being the first to pass out.

20:51.670 --> 20:54.330
Right. And she's sprawled across the whole bed.

20:54.830 --> 20:58.920
I was thinking two in the bed and
one in the futon, but it is what it is.

20:58.920 --> 21:00.670
Let's sleep in the futon.

21:00.670 --> 21:02.210
Yeah, let's do that.

21:08.130 --> 21:13.380
Hey, Hazuki. I ranked second on our finals.

21:15.670 --> 21:18.670
What? Did you want me to praise you too?

21:19.170 --> 21:20.830
Yeah, to be honest.

21:24.290 --> 21:25.670
You did great.

21:29.710 --> 21:31.790
Yeah, I did.

21:33.210 --> 21:34.540
Good night, Hazuki.

21:34.540 --> 21:36.500
Yeah, good night.

21:46.130 --> 21:48.420
I fell asleep without realizing it.

22:02.500 --> 22:06.500
I hope we all end up in the same class together.

22:11.130 --> 22:14.500
The school's shadow glows a dark red

22:14.500 --> 22:20.790
I haven't reached the end of my youth

22:21.040 --> 22:26.210
I've experienced a little bit of it, but it'll be over soon

22:26.210 --> 22:30.460
Along with the smiles you give me

22:30.460 --> 22:32.380
It's beautiful

22:32.380 --> 22:35.210
Is it okay to call this a miracle?

22:35.460 --> 22:41.130
I love, love, love these days

22:41.130 --> 22:47.580
But they won't last forever, so I tightly hold on to them

22:47.580 --> 22:51.710
Because we're kids and our spring has just begun

22:51.710 --> 22:55.080
Let's move forward, forward forward, one step at a time

22:55.080 --> 22:58.420
Now, a firm wind faintly blows

22:58.420 --> 23:06.080
I hope our time together at least colors the world a little

23:06.080 --> 23:10.710
What kind of canvas will we paint? What kind of future will we have?

23:10.710 --> 23:14.500
I don't know, but I want to believe

23:13.790 --> 23:18.080
We'll definitely smile and wave at each other

23:14.880 --> 23:17.920
We look forward to tomorrow a little

23:17.920 --> 23:21.630
When we say, "See you later" to each other

23:21.710 --> 23:28.580
With the season's quick passing, our words repeat

23:28.580 --> 23:35.000
Please, please may we be happy!
